8. Super admin dashboard (সুপার এডমিন)
Who: the owner of the whole platform. Accent: indigo. Menu order: Homepage, Admin dashboard, Notice board, Audit log.
8.1 Admin dashboard: institutions and users
• Stat cards (top row, four): total registered institutions 🏫, active ✅, pending applications ⏳ (amber tile), total students 🎓 and total users 👥. Numbers count up on load. The pending card pulses softly with an amber dot when above zero.
• Registration review table: columns প্রতিষ্ঠান, ধরন, জেলা, আবেদনের তারিখ, স্ট্যাটাস pill, actions. Buttons: অনুমোদন (gradient), স্থগিত (outline), বাতিল (red outline). Each action asks for confirmation in a small modal; the row’s pill changes colour with a 300ms cross-fade.
• Institution switcher: a dropdown plus “প্রতিষ্ঠানে প্রবেশ করুন”; once inside, a navy banner at the top of the page shows “আপনি আছেন: <প্রতিষ্ঠান>” with a button to leave.
• Add institution: button opens a modal with the registration fields.
• Delete institution: red outline button, modal requires typing the institution name to confirm.
• User and role management: tabbed table (অধ্যক্ষ, শিক্ষক, শিক্ষার্থী, অভিভাবক) with search, role pill, email, “পাসওয়ার্ড রিসেট” and মুছুন. Passwords are never displayed; only a reset action is offered.
8.2 Notice board
Compose box (title, body, audience) with a gradient “প্রকাশ করুন” button. Below it, notice cards with an 📢 tile, title, date and a delete button. New notices slide in at the top.
8.3 Audit and security log
Filter bar (user, action type, date range) above a dense table: time, user, role, action (লগইন, পরীক্ষা তৈরি, নম্বর এন্ট্রি, নম্বর পরিবর্তন), details. Rows for changes to marks use an amber left border. Log is read-only; export as CSV.
9. Principal / institution admin dashboard (অধ্যক্ষ)
Who: principal or head teacher. Accent: indigo to teal. Menu has eleven items; the academic year bar is always visible.
9.1 Overview (school control)
• Live summary cards: classes and sections 📚, subjects, students 🎓, teachers 👩‍🏫, running and published exams 📝.
• Quick action cards: seven large cards (classes and subjects, teacher assignment, student admission, create exam, marks entry, result approval, tabulation). Each has a gradient icon tile and a short line; hover lifts the card and the tile rotates 6°.
• Exam progress tracker: list of exams, each with a progress bar (Brand gradient fill) showing subjects with marks submitted out of total, and a pill (চলমান amber, প্রকাশিত green). Bars animate from 0 on load.
9.2 Classes, sections and subjects
• Left panel: class list (ষষ্ঠ, সপ্তম, নবম, দশম) with code, year, class teacher; add, edit, delete. Sections appear as chips (ক, খ, গ, বিজ্ঞান, মানবিক, ব্যবসায় শিক্ষা).
• Right panel: class and section filters above the subject table. Add-subject dialog fields: name, code, scope (all sections or a chosen section), type (আবশ্যিক or ৪র্থ বিষয়).
• Pass rule block: two radio cards. “আলাদা পাস” reveals three rows (CQ, MCQ, ব্যবহারিক) with full marks and pass marks and a “৩৩% অটো” button. “একত্রে মোট পাস” sets component pass marks to 0 and shows only the total.
9.3 Teachers and assignments
• Teacher table with name, email, phone and assigned load. “নতুন শিক্ষক” opens a wide modal: account fields (name, email, phone, password) and an assignment builder where each row is class + section (or all) + subject, with “+ আরও যোগ করুন” and “নতুন বিষয় তৈরি করুন” inline.
• Clicking a teacher opens a side drawer listing assignments as chips that can be removed. Delete account is in the drawer footer.
9.4 Students
• Admission form (modal, two columns): name, roll, student ID, class, section, year, gender, date of birth, father, mother, guardian mobile, address, 4th subject, login email and password (creates the student account).
• Bulk import: drag area for CSV or Excel, link “স্যাম্পল CSV ডাউনলোড”, preview of the first rows with errors highlighted in red before confirming.
• List: class and section filters, search by name, roll or ID, edit and delete per row.
9.5 Exam management
• Exam form: name, year, default class, section (all or one), start and end date, marks deadline.
• Mark distribution engine: a stack of rule cards. Each card: class, section, subject, then three toggles (CQ, MCQ, Practical) with full and pass marks, or total-only pass. Preset chips: সাধারণ ১০০ (70+30), ব্যবহারিক ১০০ (50+25+25), ৫০ (35+15), ৫০ ব্যবহারিক, শুধু লিখিত ১০০, শুধু MCQ ১০০, ৩৩% অটো. Clone and delete icons on each card.
• Subject combination: cards for combined papers (বাংলা ১ম+২য়, ইংরেজি ১ম+২য়, custom). Aggregation mode toggle (মোট যোগফল or গড়), pass rule select (combined total, combined components, each paper separately), and a checkbox for ৪র্থ বিষয়.
• Admit cards: appear automatically after saving. Toolbar: “সকল প্রবেশপত্র PDF” and print. Each card has its own ডাউনলোড and প্রিন্ট buttons. Card design: A4 portrait, navy header band with logo and institution name, student table, subject and marks table, signature line.
• Publish toggles: per section switch (ক, খ, whole class) with a green “প্রকাশিত” state. Delete exam uses a confirmation modal.
9.6 Marks entry and drafts
• Selectors for exam, class, section, subject in a sticky row.
• Table: roll, name, CQ, MCQ, Practical, total, grade (with point), status. Fields not in the distribution are locked with a hatched grey background. Entering more than the maximum clears the field and shows a toast. Total, grade and pass or fail update as you type.
• Footer actions: “খসড়া সংরক্ষণ” (outline) and “অনুমোদনের জন্য জমা দিন” (gradient).
9.7 Result approval and publishing
Matrix of subjects against status (প্রস্তুত count, ড্রাফট, জমা হয়েছে, অনুমোদিত). Each subject row has “অনুমোদন করুন”. Above it a publish control for the whole exam or one section, with an unpublish option, and a button to open the tabulation sheet.
9.8 Tabulation sheet
• Selectors for exam, class and section tabs (সকল, ক, খ).
• View switch: বিস্তারিত (CQ, MCQ, PR, total, grade per subject) and সংক্ষিপ্ত (total, grade, C/M/P breakdown, combined papers as 101: 75 + 102: 80).
• Final columns: GPA (including the 4th subject bonus above 2.00), overall grade, উত্তীর্ণ or অনুত্তীর্ণ pill. Failed rows have a faint red tint.
• Actions: দেখুন (single official marksheet dialog with PDF and print), বাল্ক অফিসিয়াল মার্কশিট (preview, multi-page A4 PDF, print), Excel and CSV export, print sheet.
• Marksheet design: A4 portrait, navy top band, logo left, institution and EIIN centred, student block, subject table, GPA box with the Warm accent seal, signature row for class teacher and principal.
9.9 Notice board
Same component as the super admin’s, scoped to the institution. Audience select: teachers, students, parents.
9.10 Settings
Four stacked cards: প্রতিষ্ঠানের তথ্য (name, logo, address, EIIN, principal, contact), সংখ্যা ফরম্যাট (Bangla or English switch), গ্রেডিং স্কেল (editable table A+ to F with range and point), and ৪র্থ বিষয়ের নিয়ম (base pass point 2.00, maximum bonus 3.00, and the choice of failing the exam or zeroing the bonus when the 4th subject is failed). A sticky save bar appears when anything changes.
9.11 Audit log
Same table as the super admin’s, limited to this institution.
10. Teacher dashboard (শিক্ষক)
Who: subject and class teachers. Accent: teal. Menu: Homepage, Classes and sections, Assignments, Marks entry, Notice board. Academic year bar in the top bar.
• Classes and sections: cards for each assigned class + section + subject with student count and a teal progress ring for marks submitted. Below, the student list for the chosen class (roll, ID, 4th subject, guardian info). A small “+ শিক্ষার্থী যোগ করুন” button for the teacher’s own classes.
• Assignments and homework: left list of assignments with due date pills; “নতুন অ্যাসাইনমেন্ট” form (title, description, full marks, due date, class and section). Right panel: submissions list; selecting one shows the student’s answer, a marks field and a feedback box, and “মূল্যায়ন করুন”.
• Marks entry: identical to 9.6 but the selectors only list the teacher’s own class, section and subject; everything else is hidden.
• Notice board: read all notices, publish to students.
11. Student and parent dashboard (শিক্ষার্থী ও অভিভাবক)
Who: students and parents. Accent: amber highlights on a calm layout. Menu: Homepage, My results and marksheets (parents: children’s results), My assignments, Notice board.
• Profile card (top): gradient avatar ring, name, roll, ID, class, section, year, parents, login email. Parents with several children see a pill switcher for each child.
• Admit cards: list of running and upcoming exams with “প্রবেশপত্র দেখুন”, print and PDF.
• Published results: one card per exam with GPA in a large amber number, letter grade, total marks and pass or fail pill. Expanding a card shows the subject table (CQ, MCQ, Practical, total, grade) including combined subjects, and “অফিসিয়াল মার্কশিট” for print or PDF. Results of unpublished sections never appear.
• My assignments: cards with due date and full marks. “জমা দিন” opens a text box; after grading, marks and teacher feedback appear on the same card.
• Notice board: read only.
